senses.gloss:
tūla,
(1) m. or nt. (cf. Skt. tūlikā, and Lex. tūli, tuli, f., paintbrush), an instrument for writing (Index pencil): (rātrau pradīpena Buddhavacanaṃ paṭhanti, atra bhūrjena prayojanaṃ) tailena masinā kalamayā tūlena (mss. bhū˚) Divy 〔532.11〕;
(2) some musical instrument, prob. = tūra (late and Lex. Skt., Schmidt, Nachträge; also AMg.; cf. Skt. tūrya), which should perhaps be read: vallaki-tūlāṃ Mv 〔iii.82.5〕 (vs, in list of mus. instruments; prob. acc. pl., rather than acc. sg. f.).
